HST Office: the crash handler never waits forever on the configuration.

Owner report (Windows 1.0.1, autosave every minute with "always autosave the document instead"):
closing a Writer document showed the emergency save dialog with an empty list, and the office
could only be ended from the Task Manager.

Reproduced on Windows 11 with an access violation injected into the main thread while the last
window closed. A dump of the hung process shows the main thread inside Desktop::Exception ->
FlushConfiguration -> configmgr flushModifications -> join of the "configmgrWriter" thread, and that
thread waiting in writeModFile for configmgr's lock, which the main thread still held: it faulted
inside a configuration commit (utl::ConfigManager::storeConfigItems while the frames closed). The
same join runs inside the emergency save of 1.0.2 (hstrecovery::flushConfiguration after each
copy), where it freezes the save dialog on screen, and from exit(255) of the Windows signal handler
(the configmgr singleton's destructor flushes too).

- Desktop::Exception flushes the configuration on a helper thread and goes on after 5 s.
- hstrecovery::flushConfiguration does the same; after one stuck flush the later ones are skipped.
  The recovery copies are written before any flush, so the emergency save still saves them.
- No recovery UI after Application::Quit(): every document is closed by then (hence the empty
  list) and Dialog::Execute() returns without running its loop.
- Windows: the signal handler ends the process with TerminateProcess instead of exit(), which ran
  the static destructors from inside the exception filter.
